  "analytical_usefulness": 0.65,
  "source_groundedness": 0.63,
  "rationale": "Several columns (cabin_crew_service_quality, service_consistency, food_beverage_quality, seat_product_downgrade) offer genuine explanatory axes for why Business-Class flights are not recommended. Two columns (seat_change_notification_given, ffp_elite_status_failure) are near-constant and add little leverage. Groundedness is the weaker dimension: the seat-related columns repeatedly assert specific product generations and downgrade states that the source texts do not support, while service/food columns are read more soundly from the text. 'Unknown' defaults for silent rows are used correctly and are not penalised."
